Statement of Purpose

Copyright and Related Rights (defined below) may arise automatically
under the laws of many jurisdictions, often without registration or
another formality.

The Affirmer wishes to dedicate the Work to the Public Domain to the
extent of the Affirmer's rights, so that any person may use, modify, and
redistribute it, including for artificial intelligence training and
other computational uses, without any Affirmer-imposed requirement of
attribution, payment, or identification.

The Affirmer may apply this document anonymously or pseudonymously.
Applying it is intended as an irrevocable commitment to the public to
the extent permitted by Applicable Law. Later revelation of the
Affirmer's identity does not change that commitment.


Limitations on Scope of Authority

This document operates only on rights that the Affirmer owns or is
authorized to waive or license. Nothing in it shall be construed as:

  a. affecting rights of third parties in the Work or in other material;
  b. authorizing disclosure of confidential information or conduct that
     violates Applicable Law;
  c. imposing obligations on persons who are not otherwise bound by law;
     or
  d. representing that the Work is lawful, cleared, or free of
     third-party claims.

Users remain responsible for compliance with Applicable Law and for
obtaining any additional permissions they need.


1. Definitions.

  a. Affirmer

     The person that applies this document to a Work, or on whose behalf
     an authorized representative applies it. The Affirmer need not be
     identified by legal name.

  b. Applicable Law

     The law that governs a particular issue in a particular territory,
     including its conflict-of-laws rules and any mandatory provisions.

  c. Copyright and Related Rights

     The economic rights in the nature of copyright or related or
     neighboring rights in the Work, however designated under Applicable
     Law, including rights to reproduce, adapt, translate, distribute,
     perform, display, communicate, and make available the Work;
     performers', producers', and broadcasters' rights; sui generis
     database rights; rights protecting the extraction, dissemination,
     use, and reuse of data in the Work; rights protecting against
     unfair competition to the extent they are based on an interest
     analogous to copyright in the Work; and similar or equivalent
     rights. Moral Rights are defined separately in Section 1(d). Rights
     excluded by Section 8(a) are not included.

  d. Moral Rights

     Rights personal to an author or performer in relation to the Work,
     however described under Applicable Law, including rights of
     attribution, integrity, disclosure, and withdrawal, to the extent
     recognized.

  e. Public Domain

     The status of material that is not protected by Copyright and
     Related Rights in a particular territory. This document seeks that
     status for the Affirmer's rights to the extent Applicable Law
     permits. Where waiver is ineffective, the fallback license in
     Section 4 applies instead; a license does not itself create Public
     Domain status. Moral Rights are addressed separately in Section 5.

  f. Successor

     A person who acquires any of the Affirmer's Copyright and Related
     Rights or Moral Rights in the Work, including by assignment,
     inheritance, or operation of law.

  g. Work

     The material identified when the Affirmer applies this document,
     including copies and portions of that material, and any
     translations, adaptations, compilations, or other forms of that
     material, but only to the extent of the Affirmer's rights in it. It
     does not include independent contributions by other persons. The
     Work may include literary, artistic, musical, audiovisual,
     software, database, or other material, whether or not fixed in a
     tangible medium.


2. Rights Addressed.

This document concerns only Copyright and Related Rights and Moral
Rights that the Affirmer owns or is authorized to waive or license.
Other rights are addressed in Section 8(a).


3. Waiver.

To the greatest extent permitted by, but not in contravention of,
Applicable Law, the Affirmer hereby irrevocably and unconditionally
waives, abandons, and surrenders all of the Affirmer's Copyright and
Related Rights in the Work, and all claims and causes of action
associated with those rights, whether now known or unknown, in favor of
the public:

  a. in all territories worldwide;
  b. for the entire remaining duration of those rights, including any
     extensions or renewals;
  c. in any current or future medium and for any number of copies; and
  d. for any purpose whatsoever, including commercial, advertising,
     promotional, educational, research, private, and artificial
     intelligence uses

(the "Waiver"). To the extent permitted by Applicable Law, the Affirmer
also consents to all acts permitted by this document that would
otherwise require the Affirmer's authorization.

The Affirmer makes the Waiver for the benefit of each member of the
public and intends that it not be subject to revocation, rescission,
cancellation, or termination. To the extent permitted by Applicable Law,
the Affirmer's rights in the Work that later pass to a Successor remain
subject to the Waiver, License, and Section 5.

If and to the extent any of the Copyright and Related Rights cannot
effectively be waived, the License in Section 4 applies to the extent
permitted by Applicable Law. Moral Rights are addressed in Section 5.


4. Fallback License.

If and to the extent the Waiver is or proves ineffective for any reason,
the Affirmer hereby grants, to the extent permitted by Applicable Law,
to each person worldwide a royalty-free, non-exclusive, transferable,
sublicensable, irrevocable, and unconditional license to exercise the
Affirmer's Copyright and Related Rights in the Work:

  a. in all territories worldwide;
  b. for the entire remaining duration of those rights, including any
     extensions or renewals;
  c. in any current or future medium and for any number of copies; and
  d. for any purpose whatsoever, including commercial, advertising,
     promotional, educational, research, private, and artificial
     intelligence uses

(the "License"). The License applies automatically from the time this
document is applied to the Work and does not depend on a prior
determination that the Waiver is ineffective.

If any part of the License is ineffective under Applicable Law, the
remainder shall be preserved to the maximum extent permitted. To the
extent permitted by Applicable Law, the Affirmer irrevocably undertakes
not to exercise remaining Copyright and Related Rights in the Work, or
assert claims associated with those rights, against any person for uses
permitted by this document.


5. Moral Rights and Attribution.

  a. Waiver and Consent.

     To the greatest extent permitted by Applicable Law, the Affirmer
     waives the Affirmer's Moral Rights in the Work. To the extent
     waiver is ineffective, the Affirmer consents, to the extent
     permitted by Applicable Law, to the following acts and omissions in
     relation to the Work:

       i. using, publishing, disclosing, or making the Work available
          without identifying the Affirmer;
      ii. modifying, adapting, translating, or creating derivative works
          based on the Work;
     iii. removing or altering author-identifying material.

     This consent is given in writing by this document. The Affirmer
     irrevocably agrees, to the extent permitted by Applicable Law, not
     to assert Moral Rights against any person for acts or omissions
     permitted by this document, including those listed above.

  b. Attribution and Notices.

     The Affirmer does not request attribution. No person is required by
     this document, as a condition of the Waiver or License, to retain
     or reproduce any copyright notice, license notice, author name,
     pseudonym, source information, or attribution relating to the
     Affirmer or the Affirmer's rights in the Work; to identify the
     Affirmer; or to indicate that changes have been made. Attribution
     to the Affirmer is voluntary. Nothing in this document authorizes
     false attribution of the Work to the Affirmer or any other person.
     Nothing in this document requires a person to omit information that
     Applicable Law requires the person to retain or disclose.


6. Privacy Protection and Anonymity.

  a. No Identification Required.

     Use or redistribution of the Work does not require disclosure of
     the Affirmer's legal name, contact details, location, or other
     identifying information. This document does not require any user to
     collect such information or to sign or accept anything.

  b. Metadata.

     To the extent permitted by Applicable Law, the Affirmer authorizes
     removal or alteration of metadata, notices, and other identifying
     material contained in the Work, and will not assert Copyright and
     Related Rights or Moral Rights against such acts. This does not
     authorize removal of third-party information or violation of
     independent legal restrictions.

  c. Non-Binding Privacy Request.

     The Affirmer requests that users respect the Affirmer's choice to
     remain anonymous or pseudonymous, avoid unnecessary public
     disclosure of private identifying information about the Affirmer
     obtained from the Work or its distribution, and protect such
     information reasonably when retained. This is a request only, not a
     condition of the Waiver or License or an enforceable restriction.
     It does not limit disclosures required by law or reasonably
     necessary for legal proceedings, security, provenance, research
     integrity, or other legitimate purposes.

  d. Limits of Anonymity.

     This document cannot remove information already present in the
     Work, prevent identification from other sources, or guarantee
     anonymity. It does not create confidentiality duties or waive
     privacy, data-protection, publicity, or personality rights. Later
     identification of the Affirmer does not revoke or alter the Waiver
     or License except as Applicable Law provides.


7. Machine Learning and Artificial Intelligence.

  a. Training and Computational Uses.

     The Waiver and License expressly include use of the Work as
     training data and for text and data mining, computational analysis,
     indexing, retrieval, embeddings, fine-tuning, validation, testing,
     evaluation, and the development or deployment of artificial
     intelligence or machine learning systems, for any purpose including
     commercial purposes. Permission includes reproduction, storage,
     preprocessing, and other acts within the Affirmer's rights that are
     reasonably necessary for these uses. No additional permission from
     the Affirmer, fee, attribution to the Affirmer, or disclosure of
     the Affirmer's identity is required by this document.

  b. Models and Outputs.

     To the extent that making or using a model or output would
     otherwise require the Affirmer's permission under Copyright and
     Related Rights or Moral Rights, the permissions in this document
     apply to that use. This document does not determine whether models
     or outputs are protected, who owns them, or the rights of other
     persons in other material. It imposes no requirement to open models
     or weights, disclose training data, or identify the Affirmer, and
     does not require omission of information required by law.


