9. Interpretation.

  a. No Additional Conditions.

     Requests and guidance in this document are not conditions of the
     Waiver or License. This document imposes no additional conditions
     or restrictions on the rights granted by the Affirmer. Nothing in
     this document limits rights a person already has under Applicable
     Law or separate permission, or prevents additional permissions.

  b. Liberal Construction.

     This document shall be interpreted to maximize the public's freedom
     to use the Work, consistent with the Statement of Purpose and to
     the extent permitted by Applicable Law. If a permission is
     ineffective in one form, it shall be given effect in any other form
     permitted by Applicable Law.

  c. Governing Law and Jurisdiction.

     This document is intended to operate worldwide. The law applicable
     to a particular issue, including its conflict-of-laws rules,
     determines its effect. No exclusive governing law or forum is
     designated.

  d. Language.

     This document is drafted in English. Translations are for
     convenience. The English version prevails to the extent permitted
     by Applicable Law.

  e. Persons.

     References to a person include any natural person, legal entity, or
     other organization. Words in the singular include the plural and
     vice versa unless the context requires otherwise.

  f. Successors.

     To the extent permitted by Applicable Law, the Waiver, License, and
     the Affirmer's undertakings survive transfer of the relevant rights
     and apply to Successors. A later transfer does not enlarge the
     rights transferred beyond those still held by the Affirmer, subject
